{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Wearable Device.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Wearable Device.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"wearable device wearable device","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Wearable Device.md","fileName":"Wearable Device.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Wearable Device","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-10-04 23:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Self-Tracking Markets and Institutional Power]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Self-Tracking Markets and Institutional Power","self-tracking.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Wearable Device.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Wearable Device.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"wearable device wearable device","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Wearable Device.md","fileName":"Wearable Device.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Wearable Device","heading":"Wearable Device","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A wearable device is computing equipment designed to be carried on the body, often as a watch, band, clip, garment, or accessory. It can use sensors to collect measurements while remaining integrated into ordinary movement and routines.\n\nWearability is social as well as technical. Miniaturized electronics, lower-power components, and wireless connections make the device possible, while familiar forms such as a wristwatch make it imaginable as something a person would display and repeatedly wear. Fashion, status, comfort, and workplace expectations can therefore affect adoption as much as sensor capability.\n\nA wearable may cross consumer, employment, and medical settings. Its physical form does not determine whether the collected data are harmless wellness information or consequential health and surveillance records.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Self-Tracking Markets and In